{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790408250553,"sessionID":"ses_f235c04d5ffeUJX2ap4z7696qq","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_10744126a7d640e7a6b7aa9a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","prompt":"Explore the /workspace directory thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. Read the project.godot file\n2. Read the task_config.json file\n3. List all files in assets/ directory recursively\n4. List all files in scenes/ directory recursively\n5. List all files in scripts/ directory recursively\n6. Check the .godot/ directory structure\n\nReturn all the information you find, including full file contents of project.godot, task_config.json, and any existing scene or script files.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f235b957cffexJeVqSUpbok6Id\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a complete report of the `/workspace` directory exploration.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Top-Level Structure\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/\n├── assets/\n├── scenes/\n├── scripts/\n├── project.godot\n└── task_config.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. project.godot\n\n**File:** `/workspace/project.godot`\n\n```ini\n; Engine configuration file.\n; It's best edited using the editor UI and not directly,\n; since the parameters that go here are not all obvious.\n;\n; Format:\n;   [section] ; section goes between []\n;   param=value ; assign values to parameters\n\nconfig_version=5\n\n[application]\n\nconfig/name=\"River Raid Player Jet Scene\"\nconfig/description=\"A simple task to test CUA ability to move a player asset to the origin coordinates\"\nrun/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\nconfig/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.4\")\n\n[rendering]\n\ntextures/canvas_textures/default_texture_filter=0\nrenderer/rendering_method=\"gl_compatibility\"\n```\n\nKey observations:\n- Config version 5 (Godot 4.x format).\n- Project name: \"River Raid Player Jet Scene\".\n- Main scene set to `res://scenes/main.tscn`.\n- Uses **GL Compatibility** renderer (OpenGL, suitable for 2D pixel art games).\n- Godot version feature tag: `4.4`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. task_config.json\n\n**File:** `/workspace/task_config.json`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"instruction\": \"Create a Player scene with a CharacterBody2D root named Player, add an AnimatedSprite2D that autoplay the default animation and includes looping default/left/right jet frames from assets/sprites/sprites-Sheet.png and a non-looping explode sequence from the smoke sprites at assets/sprites/Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png, and attach a 16\\u00d716 rectangular CollisionShape2D that fits the jet.\"\n}\n```\n\nThis is the task instruction for an AI/automated agent. It describes what needs to be built.\n\n---\n\n## 4. assets/ Directory (Recursive Listing)\n\n```\nassets/\n└── sprites/\n    ├── Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png\n    ├── Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png.import\n    ├── sprites-Sheet.png\n    └── sprites-Sheet.png.import\n```\n\nThere are **4 files** total -- 2 PNG sprite sheets and their corresponding Godot `.import` files.\n\n**sprites-Sheet.png.import** (`/workspace/assets/sprites/sprites-Sheet.png.import`):\n- Importer: `texture`\n- Type: `CompressedTexture2D`\n- UID: `uid://dw3plevce8glj`\n- Destination: `res://.godot/imported/sprites-Sheet.png-b788cfb551763062dd2af0c3b300f5c1.ctex`\n- Parameters: VRAM texture disabled, mipmaps disabled, fix alpha border enabled, no compression.\n\n**Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png.import** (`/workspace/assets/sprites/Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png.import`):\n- Importer: `texture`\n- Type: `CompressedTexture2D`\n- UID: `uid://dwai200lga04j`\n- Destination: `res://.godot/imported/Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png-4c283409538c90586d9ac0d48e6a66c5.ctex`\n- Same parameters as above.\n\n---\n\n## 5. scenes/ Directory (Recursive Listing)\n\n```\nscenes/\n├── main.tscn\n└── player.tscn\n```\n\n### main.tscn (`/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`)\n\n```ini\n[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3 uid=\"uid://bk0ocudwcker6\"]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"PackedScene\" uid=\"uid://bvqxo8n4xhc2j\" path=\"res://scenes/player.tscn\" id=\"1_o5qli\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Node2D\"]\n\n[node name=\"Camera2D\" type=\"Camera2D\" parent=\".\"]\nzoom = Vector2(2, 2)\n\n[node name=\"Player\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"1_o5qli\")]\n```\n\nThis is the main scene containing:\n- A root `Node2D` named \"Main\".\n- A `Camera2D` child with 2x zoom.\n- An instance of the `player.tscn` scene (external resource `1_o5qli`).\n\n### player.tscn (`/workspace/scenes/player.tscn`)\n\n```ini\n[gd_scene load_steps=5 format=3 uid=\"uid://bvqxo8n4xhc2j\"]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Texture2D\" path=\"res://assets/sprites/sprites-Sheet.png\" id=\"1_0pln3\"]\n\n[sub_resource type=\"AtlasTexture\" id=\"AtlasTexture_default\"]\natlas = ExtResource(\"1_0pln3\")\nregion = Rect2(16, 0, 16, 16)\n\n[sub_resource type=\"SpriteFrames\" id=\"SpriteFrames_player\"]\nanimations = [{\n\"frames\": [{\n\"duration\": 1.0,\n\"texture\": SubResource(\"AtlasTexture_default\")\n}],\n\"loop\": true,\n\"name\": &\"default\",\n\"speed\": 5.0\n}]\n\n[node name=\"Player\" type=\"CharacterBody2D\"]\n\n[node name=\"AnimatedSprite2D\" type=\"AnimatedSprite2D\" parent=\".\"]\nsprite_frames = SubResource(\"SpriteFrames_player\")\n```\n\nThis is the Player scene -- currently in a partial/incomplete state:\n- Root node: `CharacterBody2D` named \"Player\" (**matches task spec**).\n- An `AnimatedSprite2D` child with `SpriteFrames_player`:\n  - Has only a **\"default\" animation** (looping, 1 frame, speed 5.0).\n  - The default frame uses an `AtlasTexture` from region `Rect2(16, 0, 16, 16)` of the sprites sheet.\n- **Missing from the task spec:**\n  - No `collision_shape_2d` node (no `CollisionShape2D` with 16x16 rectangle).\n  - No \"left\" or \"right\" animations.\n  - No \"explode\" animation (from the smoke sprite sheet).\n  - The scene references `sprites-Sheet.png` but does **not** yet reference `Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. scripts/ Directory\n\nThe `scripts/` directory exists but is **empty** -- no script files (`.gd` or otherwise) found.\n\n---\n\n## 7. .godot/ Directory Structure\n\n```\n.godot/\n├── .gdignore\n├── editor/\n│   ├── filesystem_cache10\n│   ├── main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg\n│   └── project_metadata.cfg\n├── global_script_class_cache.cfg\n├── imported/\n│   ├── Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png-4c283409538c90586d9ac0d48e6a66c5.ctex\n│   ├── Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png-4c283409538c90586d9ac0d48e6a66c5.md5\n│   ├── sprites-Sheet.png-b788cfb551763062dd2af0c3b300f5c1.ctex\n│   └── sprites-Sheet.png-b788cfb551763062dd2af0c3b300f5c1.md5\n├── scene_groups_cache.cfg\n└── uid_cache.bin\n```\n\n**Files and their contents:**\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `.gdignore` | Empty file -- tells Godot to ignore this directory for resource imports. |\n| `global_script_class_cache.cfg` | Contains `list=[]` -- no global script classes registered. |\n| `scene_groups_cache.cfg` | Empty file -- no scene groups defined. |\n| `uid_cache.bin` | Binary file -- stores resource UID mappings. |\n| **editor/project_metadata.cfg** | Git editor executable path: `/run/gamedevbench-bin/godot`. Recent files: `main.tscn`. |\n| **editor/filesystem_cache10** | FS cache listing all project resources, their types, timestamps, UIDs, and dependencies. |\n| **editor/main.tscn-folding-3ad5c...cfg** | Code folding state (all empty). |\n| **imported/*.ctex** (2 files) | Compiled/compressed texture files for the two sprite sheets. |\n| **imported/*.md5** (2 files) | MD5 hash files for detecting texture changes. |\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Project State\n\nThis is a **Godot 4.4 project** set up for an AI agent task (\"River Raid Player Jet Scene\"). The project has:\n\n1. **Two sprite sheets**: a jet sprites sheet (`sprites-Sheet.png`) and a smoke FX sheet (`Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png`), both imported as compressed textures.\n2. **A main scene** (`main.tscn`) with a `Node2D` root, a 2x-zoomed `Camera2D`, and an instance of the Player scene.\n3. **A partially built Player scene** (`player.tscn`) with a `CharacterBody2D` root and an `AnimatedSprite2D` that only has a single-frame \"default\" animation -- it still needs:\n   - `left` and `right` animations (looping jet frames from `sprites-Sheet.png`)\n   - An `explode` animation (non-looping smoke frames from `Free Smoke Fx  Pixel 04.png`)\n   - A `CollisionShape2D` with a 16x16 rectangle\n4. **An empty `scripts/` directory** -- no game logic scripts exist yet.\n5. The `.godot/` directory has standard Godot editor cache and imported texture data.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f235c04d5ffeUJX2ap4z7696qq","sessionId":"ses_f235b957cffexJeVqSUpbok6Id","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790408157831,"end":1790408250541}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_3fc0c1f0-727e-4f2f-949f-4ca8b1209704"}},"id":"prt_0dca46a79001fLuUI1suoemB9E","sessionID":"ses_f235c04d5ffeUJX2ap4z7696qq","messageID":"msg_0dca42f62001y3UWpvmHH72jTi"}}
